From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v8-embed-feedstock <noreply@github.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let the inspector config name its own protocol file

On Windows the inspector protocol generator dies before generating
anything:

  File "deps/v8/third_party/inspector_protocol/code_generator.py",
    line 373, in __init__
      self.generate_domains = self.read_protocol_file(config.protocol.path)
  AttributeError: 'X' object has no attribute 'path'

inspector_protocol_config.json has no "path" key.  config.protocol.path
exists only because v8.gyp passes it on the command line:

  '--config_value', 'protocol.path=<(v8_inspector_js_protocol)',

and on Windows that value does not take effect.  The command is not
truncated: --inspector_protocol_dir, a required argument that comes after
--config_value in the action, was accepted, or argparse would have failed
long before line 373.  So the value arrives but does not parse -- and the
generator discards a config value it cannot split cleanly without saying
so:

  parts = key_value.split("=")   # splits on every '='
  if len(parts) == 2:            # anything else: dropped, no error

Rather than depend on an argument a build system can mangle, the config
file names its own protocol file.  The two resolve to the same path -- the
JSON value is joined with the config file's directory by
code_generator.py's json_object_hook, so ../../include/js_protocol.pdl
from deps/v8/src/inspector is deps/v8/include/js_protocol.pdl, which is
what <(v8_inspector_js_protocol) expands to -- so nothing changes on the
platforms where the argument does work: there the command-line value
overrides the identical JSON one.
---
 deps/v8/src/inspector/inspector_protocol_config.json | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/deps/v8/src/inspector/inspector_protocol_config.json b/deps/v8/src/inspector/inspector_protocol_config.json
--- a/deps/v8/src/inspector/inspector_protocol_config.json
+++ b/deps/v8/src/inspector/inspector_protocol_config.json
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 {
     "protocol": {
+        "path": "../../include/js_protocol.pdl",
         "package": "src/inspector/protocol",
         "output": "protocol",
         "namespace": ["v8_inspector", "protocol"],
